# Container-scan exceptions (aquasecurity/trivy; ci-security "container" job, Plan 0005 slice 2).
#
# The CI gate fails on CRITICAL/HIGH findings (fixed or not). Findings below that
# threshold are still reported in the uploaded JSON artefact and classified in
# docs/quality/security.md (Supply chain → Container image). Nothing is listed here without
# an ID, a rationale and a review trigger; an empty list means no exception is in force.
#
# Format: one CVE/advisory id per line, preceded by a comment with the classification.

# CVE-2026-84782 — libssl3 3.0.20-1~deb12u2 (OpenSSL), HIGH, Debian status `affected`
# (no fixed version), first reported by the 2026-10-05 scan. NOT APPLICABLE to the
# process: ledger-server, ledger-admin and ledger-projector use rustls/aws-lc-rs (no
# openssl crate in Cargo.lock; deny.toml bans it); `readelf -d` NEEDED on all three is
# libgcc_s, libm, libc, ld-linux only and none references libssl/libcrypto. The library is
# present only because gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12 ships it. The premise is CI-enforced:
# scripts/check-runtime-linkage.sh (ci-security, container job) fails if any shipped
# binary's NEEDED entries name libssl/libcrypto. Review trigger: a Debian 12
# fix (then refresh the distroless digest and remove this line), any distroless base
# refresh, or any dependency that would link OpenSSL.
CVE-2026-84782
